# Concept library grain

Lecture titles are not concept ids. One calendar slot may tag several nodes.

**Split** independently citable named results, even if they share a lecture: LLN vs CLT, Markov vs Chebyshev, BFS vs DFS, Dijkstra vs Bellman–Ford. A known mix-up is a reason to split (with `seeAlso`), not to mash. Each result can carry its own theorem pass.

**Combine** only faces of one object (PMF and CDF), duals of one operator (Adam/Eve), or a **family bucket** whose children are the named members (`limit-theorems` → `lln`, `clt`).

Do not name a leaf `LLN and CLT`. `fusedCitableResults` in `server/conceptShape.ts` must stay empty for every catalog row.
